Before writing any architecture, workflow, or UI code, you MUST actively open and read the following files:

1. `agents.md`: Read this for all backend, database, testing, and PR workflow constraints. (Note: on case-sensitive systems, this may be `AGENTS.md`).
2. `DESIGN.md`: Read this for all Neo-Brutalist UI/UX specifications, layouts, and component behaviors.

UI Implementation Strictness:
- Do not invent hex colors, typography, border radius, or spacing values.
- You must strictly use the specific design tokens explicitly defined in `DESIGN.md`.
